      "name": "Product Comparison",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Which Rangefinder is Right For You?",
        "subheading": "From fast, accurate optics to fully connected shot intelligence — compare our rangefinder lineup and choose the one that fits how you play.",
        "disclaimer": ""
      }
    },
    "new_faq_section_ETa8r8": {
      "type": "new-faq-section",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_yHkcLL": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Captain Air tournament legal?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Captain Air includes a Slope Mode that can be turned off using the external slope switch, making it fully compliant for tournament play.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_NnF4xe": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I see True Distance™ yardages in my rangefinder?",
            "answer": "<p>True Distance™ yardages are controlled through the app and need to be turned on before they appear in the device’s reticle.<br/>To enable it:</p><ol><li>Start a round in the GAME App</li><li>Open the menu (top corner / hamburger menu)</li><li>Toggle True Distance™ on</li></ol><p>Once enabled, your rangefinder will display adjusted yardages directly in the reticle when you’re ranging targets.<br/>If you don’t see adjusted distances, it usually means the toggle is off — not that the feature isn’t working.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_QgxdKz": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens if I lose it on the course?",
            "answer": "<p>Captain Air includes “Find My Rangefinder” through the GAME App.<br/>If it gets left behind, you can check its last known location directly from your phone, making it much easier to recover.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_bX9Xzx": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if I don’t want all the connected or AI features?",
            "answer": "<p>No problem at all. Captain Air works perfectly as a simple point-and-shoot laser rangefinder right out of the box.<br/>All connected features are optional — you can use it traditionally or unlock more functionality when you’re ready.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_DkeQKP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are the numbers shown in photos exactly what I’ll see through the viewfinder?",
            "answer": "<p>In-use product images are designed to reflect the red display color customers see through the device. Some marketing images use enlarged graphic numbers to make distances and key data easier to read online.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_FqRXap": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the IP65 rating actually mean?",
            "answer": "<p>IP65 means the device is protected against dust and water from any direction.<br/>In real terms, it’s built to handle steady rain, wet carts, early morning dew, and gritty conditions without affecting performance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6cPBVM": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the flag-locking technology work?",
            "answer": "<p>Captain Air uses rapid targeting with built-in Pulse Vibration feedback.<br/>When you lock onto the flag, you’ll feel a quick pulse — confirming you’ve hit the pin, not the background.<br/><br/>It’s especially helpful for:</p><ul><li>Shaky hands</li><li>Busy backgrounds (trees, bunkers)</li><li>Long-distance shots</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_JtCqXY": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do Club Recommendations work?",
            "answer": "<p>When you connect to the GAME App, you’ll start with default club distances.<br/>From there:</p><ul><li>You can manually adjust your yardages</li><li>Over time, the system learns from your rounds</li><li>Data from gameplay and Rainmaker sessions refines recommendations</li></ul><p>It evolves from general guidance into personalized, data-driven club selection.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WMNXVK": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What’s the difference between Captain Air and Captain Pro?",
            "answer": "<p>Captain Air is designed to give you everything you need — and then some — in a simple, accessible package.<br/><br/>If you want:</p><ul><li>Stronger optics</li><li>Sharper display clarity</li><li>More customization</li></ul><p><strong>Then Captain Pro is the upgrade.</strong></p><p>Air keeps it clean and capable. Pro takes it to the next level.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
